## Mode 5 — Add to Todo (`add_to_todo`)

**Goal:** when the user wants something on their **Todo** backlog, **create a new card** on the **Todo** list (do **not** update Nightly; do **not** update an existing Todo card unless the user explicitly says **update todo**).

### 5.1 — Trigger

Run Mode 5 when the user says **add to todo**, **put on todo**, **todo:**, or similar with a task description.

**Do not** confuse with `todo_cards` (Mode 3) — that is **read-only list**.

### 5.2 — Get input and polish title

- Use the user’s message plus **conversation context** (branch, Jira key, chat).
- **Fix English** (B2 / B2+); preserve meaning; do not invent scope.
- **Jira-linked tasks:** apply **Jira-linked card title pattern** — typically `vap-XXXX <short Jira title>` with optional ` > ` note if the user gave extra context (e.g. `vap-1234 Short title > follow up after release`).
- **Non-Jira tasks:** one clear polished line (e.g. `Review Command Center PRD with Ali`).
- **Always create** — new card on **Todo**; add at top of list if the API allows, otherwise default position.

### 5.3 — Proceed vs AskQuestion

For duplicate checks, fetch **Todo only** — same single-list rule as Mode 4 (do not scan the whole board).

**Proceed without AskQuestion** when:

- The task text is clear (what to do is understandable).
- For `vap-xxxx`, Jira short title is resolved or obvious from context.
- No duplicate ambiguity (see below).

**Use AskQuestion** when:

- Task is too vague to title (e.g. “add that to todo” with no referent).
- **Same ticket** already exists on **Todo** and it is unclear whether to add a **second** card or skip.
- Multiple different tasks in one message and unclear which to add.
- User says **edit** / **cancel**.

When asking, offer: **Create on Todo** (show proposed title) / **Edit first** / **Cancel**.

### 5.4 — Write to Trello

1. Resolve **board** and **Todo** `listId`.
2. **Create** via MCP or REST `POST /1/cards` with polished `name`, `idList`.
3. Confirm: **action** (created), **card title**, **list** (Todo), **shortUrl**.

